{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Completion state\n\nThis workflow migration is complete. Gerrit changes 1538, 1540, and 1541 are merged. The current tree is the intended post-migration state:\n\n- .github/workflows/reconcile-bridge.yml delegates one strict synchronous commit-and-push action to the core bridge runner while preserving the exact bot identity and commit subject.\n- .github/workflows/reconcile-bridge-canary.yml delegates one strict synchronous push-only action to rebar._store.push.\n- Both workflow-local CAS loops and the reconciler raw-git exemption are absent.\n- Core owns retry/CAS recovery and workflow calls remain red on exhausted delivery.\n- Python library and MCP defaults remain best-effort; this ticket changes only the strict workflow adapters.\n- Older workflows and environments continue through the retained legacy reconcile and push contracts.\n- The stale synthetic test rationale was replaced by the generic reviewed-fixture wording in Gerrit 1541; there is no remaining implementation task.\n\n## Verification\n\nRepository checks at merged ref 694cf894def36241724e7049e3308d782037ef6d:\n- execute the focused workflow and raw-git lint suites plus make lint;\n- confirm both workflow run blocks contain one core push entrypoint and no inline fetch/merge/retry loop;\n- confirm tests/unit/test_raw_git_write_lint.py contains the generic reviewed-workflow rationale;\n- confirm rtk proxy rg -n \"4c4f|keeps the CAS loop in YAML\" tests/unit/test_raw_git_write_lint.py returns no match;\n- execute the real-git workflow smoke tests for successful delivery and rejected-push red failure.\n\nThe change rides existing locked core operations and introduces no new retry/cache/composed write, so existing push contention suites remain the correct concurrency oracle.\n\n## Compatibility and rollback\n\nThe migration centralizes delivery mechanics without narrowing any public surface. CLI workflow adapters use strict delivery; Python and MCP retain best-effort defaults. Exact reconciler identity/subject and older vocabulary remain available. Reverting the workflow call sites restores the prior inline loops and requires no data migration; pending local commits remain recoverable.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [x] Both inline workflow CAS loops are absent.\n- [x] Each workflow invokes exactly one complete core push action.\n- [x] Strict workflow delivery remains synchronous and red on exhausted failure.\n- [x] Python library and MCP push defaults remain best-effort.\n- [x] Reconciler author identity and exact commit subject are preserved.\n- [x] The reconciler raw-git exemption is removed.\n- [x] Standing decisions and executable tests state that core owns retry/CAS recovery.\n- [x] Real-git workflow smoke tests preserve successful delivery and rejected-push failure.\n- [x] Copied-template migration, timing, and rollback continuity are documented.\n- [x] tests/unit/test_raw_git_write_lint.py contains no stale ticket-4c4f CAS-loop rationale.\n- [x] [operator-attested] Gerrit changes 1538, 1540, and 1541 passed LLM-Review +1, Verified +1, and zero unresolved comments before merge.\n  provenance: environment=Gerrit and GitHub Actions runs 31241954882, 31243115851, and 31269583553; principal=project review and CI bots; privilege_posture=production-equivalent; instrument=live-call — the actual project review and CI systems evaluated the merged workflow changes."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1786442576870951001,"uuid":"88fb0d29-efea-4f0a-a124-32cf46f0f231"}